From: Gianluca Mazza <info@gianlucamazza.it>
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: apq8064: add the vendor PVS voltage boost to
 the CPU OPPs

The downstream acpuclock-8064 driver adds a 25 mV "boost" to every CPU
voltage level for all PVS bins except the slowest one of each speed bin
(pvs_tables[].boost_uv, enable_boost defaults to true). The OPP table was
transcribed from the per-level vdd_core values only, so every level ran
25 mV below what the vendor kernel uses.

On a Nexus 7 2013 (speed bin 14, PVS 6) this left 1512 MHz at 987.5 mV.
Under sustained load on all four cores, with the SoC warm, the tablet
locked up silently. Add the boost to the speed0 PVS1/3/4 and speed14
PVS1..6 columns so the voltages match the vendor tables.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
